{
  "summary": "Restricts wallet rebroadcasting and startup mempool re-addition to transactions that spend wallet inputs. Unconfirmed transactions that merely pay the wallet without spending any of its inputs will no longer be periodically rebroadcast or reloaded into the mempool on startup or import.",
  "problem": "Nodes leak network identity when passively running a wallet, because receiving transactions with low fees will cause the recipient node to rebroadcast them after 24 hours. Attackers can intentionally send low-fee transactions to target addresses and observe which node rebroadcasts or retains them, linking IP addresses to wallet ownership.",
  "evidence": [
    "Fixes #3828 ('Clients leak IPs if they are recipients of a transaction'), open since 2014.",
    "PR author notes that 'anyone can generate these, choose a low fee, and observe who rebroadcasts them' and active probing can detect nodes retaining dropped transactions."
  ],
