  "card": "Restricts wallet rebroadcasting and mempool re-addition on startup solely to transactions that spend wallet inputs. Currently, nodes passively rebroadcast incoming transactions that pay them, enabling third parties to identify a wallet node's IP address by sending low-fee transactions and watching the P2P network for rebroadcasts. This resolves long-standing issue #3828, accepting the tradeoff that recipients must manually resubmit stuck incoming transactions if the sender fails to rebroadcast.",
